osure. This move is part of Bitget’s broader push to merge crypto and traditional equity trading within a single account, reflecting a growing trend among trading platforms.\\n\\nThe launch comes as exchanges race to integrate tokenized and traditional stock trading into their ecosystems. Bitget’s Stock+ arrives just weeks after the exchange introduced **rToken**, its own tokenized stocks protocol, which has already listed over 500 US stocks and ETFs, including SpaceX, Tesla, and NVIDIA, with assets under management exceeding $50 million. However, Stock+ differentiates itself by offering **real share ownership** through brokers like RQD Clearing and Atomic Vaults Securities, rather than blockchain-based representations.\\n\\n\\n## How Stock+ Works for Crypto Users\\n\\nStock+ simplifies the process of moving from crypto to equities. Users fund their Bitget accounts with digital assets, convert them into USDC, and purchase listed shares directly. Trades are executed during US market hours, including pre-market, regular, and after-hours sessions, and users are eligible for cash dividends and stock split adjustments. Bitget also supports inbound transfers from participating brokers, allowing users to consolidate existing US equity holdings on the platform.\\n\\n\\\"Access is important, but ownership matters too,\\\" said Bitget CEO Gracy Chen in a statement. The feature is positioned as a bridge between crypto and traditional finance, enabling seamless transitions for traders.\\n\\nPromotional launch fees start at **0.1%**, with a 50% discount available until August 31. This pricing is part of a marketing push to attract users to the new offering.\\n\\n\\n## Why This Matters for Crypto and Stock Markets\\n\\nBitget’s Stock+ is part of a broader industry shift as crypto exchanges expand into traditional equities. Platforms like Coinbase and Kraken have sought regulatory approval to offer tokenized stock trading, while traditional venues like Nasdaq have launched pilots for tokenized equities. However, most of these efforts focus on **tokenized representations** of stocks, which still face regulatory uncertainty. Stock+ circumvents some of these challenges by settling real shares through regulated brokers.\\n\\nThis approach has trade-offs. While it avoids the regulatory gray area of tokenization, it also ties the product to conventional clearing systems rather than blockchain rails. For users, this means **direct ownership** but also reliance on traditional brokers for settlement and custody.\\n\\nThe launch of Stock+ reflects a growing demand for hybrid trading solutions that allow users to move seamlessly between crypto and equities. As exchanges like Bitget expand their offerings, the line between crypto platforms and traditional brokerages continues to blur.\\n\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nBitget’s Stock+ feature represents a significant step in merging crypto and traditional finance, offering users direct ownership of US-listed shares through regulated brokers. While the product leverages conventional clearing systems, it provides a clear alternative to tokenized stocks, which remain under regulatory scrutiny. With competitive fees and a focus on accessibility, Stock+ could attract crypto users looking to diversify into equities without leaving their preferred platform.\\n\\n\\n## FAQs\\n\\n**1. What is Bitget Stock+?**\\n\\nBitget Stock+ is a feature that allows users to buy real shares in US-listed companies using USDC and other digital assets. Unlike tokenized stocks, Stock+ provides direct ownership of the underlying shares through regulated US brokers.\\n\\n\\n**2. How does Stock+ differ from Bitget’s rToken?**\\n\\nWhile rToken offers tokenized exposure to equities on the blockchain, Stock+ provides **real share ownership** through regulated brokers. This means users hold actual shares, eligible for dividends and stock splits, rather than synthetic representations.\\n\\n\\n**3. What are the fees for using Stock+?**\\n\\nBitget is offering promotional launch fees starting at **0.1%**, with a 50% discount available until August 31.\\n\\n\\n**4. Can I transfer existing US equity holdings to Bitget?**\\n\\nYes, Stock+ supports inbound transfers from participating brokers, allowing users to consolidate their US equity holdings on the Bitget platform.\\n\\n\\n**5. Are there any regulatory concerns with Stock+?**\\n\\nStock+ settles real shares through regulated US brokers, avoiding some of the regulatory uncertainties associated with tokenized stocks. However, users should be aware that ownership claims rely on the broker relationships rather than the exchange itself.\\n\\n\\n**6. Which brokers does Stock+ use?**\\n\\nBitget has partnered with regulated brokers including **RQD Clearing** and **Atomic Vaults Securities** to execute trades and handle settlement for Stock+.\\n\\n\\n**Sources:**\\n- Finance Magnates: [https://www.financemagnates.com/cryptocurrency/bitget-adds-real-us-stock-ownership-to-crypto-accounts-with-stock-launch/](https://www.financemagnates.com/cryptocurrency/bitget-adds-real-us-stock-ownership-to-crypto-accounts-with-stock-launch/)\\n\\n[Word Count: 1098]\"}\n<<<END_UNTRUSTED_CHILD_RESULT>>>\n\nStats: runtime 9s • tokens 17.4k (in 15.9k / out 1.6k)\n\nAction:\nConvert this completion into a concise internal orchestration update for your parent agent in your own words. Keep this internal context private (don't mention system/log/stats/session details or announce type). If this result is duplicate or no update is needed, reply ONLY: NO_REPLY.\n<<<END_OPENCLAW_INTERNAL_CONTEXT>>>"}],"timestamp":1782115573945,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:writer:subagent:8515e93f-657e-4148-b811-5f513dec8104","sourceChannel":"webchat","sourceTool":"subagent_announce"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writer completed. Now running sync and checks..."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse6Z7GMGboPdL9DbIl05ebUD","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh\nexport RUN_DIR=\"/tmp/coinography-run-20260622-072238-13959-12593\"\nexport PIPELINE_MANIFEST\n\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/verify_artifacts.py \\\n  --stage pre_sync --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\"\n\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/sync_article_from_raw.py \\\n  --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":47948,"output":125,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48073,"cost":{"input":0.047948,"output":0.0004,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.048347999999999995}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782115573981,"responseId":"c74cc893-ca99-424d-adce-36e1e5deb4de"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tooluse6Z7GMGboPdL9DbIl05ebUD","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ARTIFACTS_FAIL: article/raw.md is empty — writer did not write the file this run\nARTICLE_INVALID: article/raw.md is empty — writer did not write the file\n\n(Command exited with code 1)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782115585046},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The writer output shows the content but didn't actually write to the file. Let me write it directly:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse1ykL2bh8UGe7KzQM89O2lU","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh\nexport RUN_DIR=\"/tmp/coinography-run-20260622-072238-13959-12593\"\n\n# Write the article directly from the writer's output\ncat > \"$RUN_DIR/article/raw.md\" << 'ARTICLE_EOF'\nMETA\n- SEO Title: Bitget Stock+ Lets Users Buy Real US Shares with USDC, Fees Start at 0.1%\n- Meta Description: Bitget Stock+ lets crypto users buy real US-listed shares with USDC, offering direct ownership through regulated brokers and 0.1% launch fees until August.\n- URL Slug: bitget-stock-plus-real-us-shares-usdc\n- Categories: Adoption, DeFi, Crypto Market News\n- Primary Keyword: Bitget Stock+\n- Secondary Keywords: USDC stock trading, crypto to equities, Bitget Stocks 2.0, tokenized stocks\n---\n\n# Bitget Stock+ Lets Crypto Users Buy Real US Shares with USDC\n\nCrypto exchange Bitget has launched **Stock+**, a feature that allows users to buy shares in US-listed companies using USDC and other digital assets. The product routes orders through regulated US brokers, granting holders direct ownership of the underlying shares rather than synthetic or derivative exposure. This move is part of Bitget's broader push to merge crypto and traditional equity trading within a single account, reflecting a growing trend among trading platforms.\n\nThe launch comes as exchanges race to integrate tokenized and traditional stock trading into their ecosystems. Bitget's Stock+ arrives just weeks after the exchange introduced **rToken**, its own tokenized stocks protocol, which has already listed over 500 US stocks and ETFs, including SpaceX, Tesla, and NVIDIA, with assets under management exceeding $50 million. However, Stock+ differentiates itself by offering **real share ownership** through brokers like RQD Clearing and Atomic Vaults Securities, rather than blockchain-based representations.\n\n\n## How Stock+ Works for Crypto Users\n\nStock+ simplifies the process of moving from crypto to equities. Users fund their Bitget accounts with digital assets, convert them into USDC, and purchase listed shares directly. Trades are executed during US market hours, including pre-market, regular, and after-hours sessions, and users are eligible for cash dividends and stock split adjustments. Bitget also supports inbound transfers from participating brokers, allowing users to consolidate existing US equity holdings on the platform.\n\n\"Access is important, but ownership matters too,\" said Bitget CEO Gracy Chen in a statement. The feature is positioned as a bridge between crypto and traditional finance, enabling seamless transitions for traders.\n\nPromotional launch fees start at **0.1%**, with a 50% discount available until August 31. This pricing is part of a marketing push to attract users to the new offering.\n\n\n## Why This Matters for Crypto and Stock Markets\n\nBitget's Stock+ is part of a broader industry shift as crypto exchanges expand into traditional equities. Platforms like Coinbase and Kraken have sought regulatory approval to offer tokenized stock trading, while traditional venues like Nasdaq have launched pilots for tokenized equities. However, most of these efforts focus on **tokenized representations** of stocks, which still face regulatory uncertainty. Stock+ circumvents some of these challenges by settling real shares through regulated brokers.\n\nThis approach has trade-offs. While it avoids the regulatory gray area of tokenization, it also ties the product to conventional clearing systems rather than blockchain rails. For users, this means **direct ownership** but also reliance on traditional brokers for settlement and custody.\n\nThe launch of Stock+ reflects a growing demand for hybrid trading solutions that allow users to move seamlessly between crypto and equities. As exchanges like Bitget expand their offerings, the line between crypto platforms and traditional brokerages continues to blur.\n\n\n## Conclusion\n\nBitget's Stock+ feature represents a significant step in merging crypto and traditional finance, offering users direct ownership of US-listed shares through regulated brokers. While the product leverages conventional clearing systems, it provides a clear alternative to tokenized stocks, which remain under regulatory scrutiny. With competitive fees and a focus on accessibility, Stock+ could attract crypto users looking to diversify into equities without leaving their preferred platform.\n\n\n## FAQs\n\n**1. What is Bitget Stock+?**\n\nBitget Stock+ is a feature that allows users to buy real shares in US-listed companies using USDC and other digital assets. Unlike tokenized stocks, Stock+ provides direct ownership of the underlying shares through regulated US brokers.\n\n\n**2. How does Stock+ differ from Bitget's rToken?**\n\nWhile rToken offers tokenized exposure to equities on the blockchain, Stock+ provides **real share ownership** through regulated brokers. This means users hold actual shares, eligible for dividends and stock splits, rather than synthetic representations.\n\n\n**3. What are the fees for using Stock+?**\n\nBitget is offering promotional launch fees starting at **0.1%**, with a 50% discount available until August 31.\n\n\n**4. Can I transfer existing US equity holdings to Bitget?**\n\nYes, Stock+ supports inbound transfers from participating brokers, allowing users to consolidate their US equity holdings on the Bitget platform.\n\n\n**5. Are there any regulatory concerns with Stock+?**\n\nStock+ settles real shares through regulated US brokers, avoiding some of the regulatory uncertainties associated with tokenized stocks. However, users should be aware that ownership claims rely on the broker relationships rather than the exchange itself.\n\n\n**6. Which brokers does Stock+ use?**\n\nBitget has partnered with regulated brokers including **RQD Clearing** and **Atomic Vaults Securities** to execute trades and handle settlement for Stock+.\n\n\n**Sources:**\n- Finance Magnates: [https://www.financemagnates.com/cryptocurrency/bitget-adds-real-us-stock-ownership-to-crypto-accounts-with-stock-launch/](https://www.financemagnates.com/cryptocurrency/bitget-adds-real-us-stock-ownership-to-crypto-accounts-with-stock-launch/)\n\n[Word Count: 1098]\nARTICLE_EOF\n\nls -la \"$RUN_DIR/article/raw.md\"\nwc -w \"$RUN_DIR/article/raw.md\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":48134,"output":1290,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49424,"cost":{"input":0.048133999999999996,"output":0.004128000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.052261999999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1782115585048,"resp